---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { PRIVACY_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description={PRIVACY_DESCRIPTION}
		/>
	</head>
	<body class="privacy-page">
		<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
		<SiteHeader />
		<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" data-reveal>
			<p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
			<h1>Privacy policy.</h1>
			<p class="lead">
				Petalwake Studios values thoughtful, respectful communication. This policy explains how we
				collect, use, and protect information shared through our website and contact form.
			</p>

			<section>
				<h2>1. Information collected through the contact form</h2>
				<p>
					When you use the contact form, we collect the information you provide: your name, email
					address, the inquiry topic, and the message text. We also process a Cloudflare Turnstile
					verification token to help reduce automated spam. The Worker reads the connecting IP address
					provided by Cloudflare; it sends that address to Turnstile for verification and uses it as the
					key for the contact endpoint's rate limit. The IP address is not included in the email.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>2. Purpose of collection</h2>
				<p>
					We use this information to respond to your inquiry, route the message to the appropriate
					studio contact, and maintain a respectful and secure communication process. We do not use
					your information for marketing unless you explicitly ask us to stay in touch.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>3. Email delivery and third-party processing</h2>
				<p>
					The form sends messages to a fixed studio destination through Resend, our transactional email
					provider. The address you provide is used as the Reply-To address. Resend processes the
					message to deliver it and may retain it according to its own terms and our account settings.
					The Worker does not save submitted messages to a site database.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>4. CAPTCHA and bot protection</h2>
				<p>
					We load Cloudflare Turnstile on the contact page. After submission, the Worker sends the
					one-time verification token and connecting IP address to Cloudflare Siteverify. A message is
					accepted only when Cloudflare reports success and the response hostname and contact action
					match. Tokens expire after a short period and cannot be reused.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>5. Website hosting and infrastructure</h2>
				<p>
					The site and contact endpoint run on Cloudflare Workers. Cloudflare's rate-limiting service
					uses the connecting IP as a short-window counter key. These counters are approximate and
					maintained per Cloudflare location; they are not a worldwide duplicate-message database.
					Cloudflare may process operational and security data as part of hosting and service delivery.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>6. Cookies and local storage</h2>
				<p>
					The site does not set first-party cookies or use session storage. It saves your language choice
					under <code>petalwake-language</code> and appearance choice under
					<code>petalwake-appearance</code> in your browser's local storage. The contact page loads
					Turnstile, and the film player loads a YouTube privacy-enhanced embed only after you choose to
					play it. Those third-party services may process browser or device information and use storage
					under their own policies.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>7. Analytics</h2>
				<p>
					This website does not currently include advertising, analytics, or behavioral tracking
					scripts. The site does not use a tracking-based consent banner.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>8. Embedded third-party content</h2>
				<p>
					The film video is not loaded until you activate its play button. It then uses YouTube's
					privacy-enhanced <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code> embed. Following external YouTube links
					also takes you to YouTube. Once loaded or visited, YouTube processes information according to
					its own policies; we do not control its storage or retention.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>9. Data retention and security</h2>
				<p>
					The Worker processes the submitted fields in memory while validating and forwarding the
					request; it does not write message content to a site database or include it in application
					error logs. Cloudflare handles the rate-limit counters, and Resend handles the delivered email;
					the single-use Turnstile token and request limit also help prevent rapid duplicate submissions.
					Their retention is governed by their services and account settings. We do not specify a
					retention period or promise deletion from those third-party systems.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>10. Your rights and contact</h2>
				<p>
					If you have a question or request about information you submitted, please use the contact
					form. Requests involving information held by Cloudflare or Resend may also be subject to those
					providers' processes. We cannot promise deletion from third-party systems through this form.
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<SiteFooter />
	</body>
</html>
